# User — OSS Claw

Personal identity and local configuration. This file is gitignored —
each contributor maintains their own copy.

## Setup

```bash
cp USER.md.template USER.md
# Edit USER.md with your identity and local paths
```

---

## Identity

Used for git commits, sign-offs, PR descriptions, and patch headers.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Name** | Your Full Name |
| **Email** | your.email@example.com |
| **GitHub username** | your-github-username |
| **JIRA username** | your-jira-username (for Apache projects) |

## Git Config

The agent uses these values for `--author` and `-c user.name`/`-c user.email`
on every commit command:

```
git -c user.name="Your Full Name" -c user.email="your.email@example.com" \
    commit -s --author="Your Full Name <your.email@example.com>" -m '...'
```

## Local Repo Paths

Where each project is cloned on your machine. The agent uses these to
`cd` into the correct directory before running commands.

| Project | Local Path |
|---------|-----------|
| Apache Hadoop | ~/oss/hadoop |
| Apache Spark | ~/oss/spark |
| Apache Airflow | ~/oss/airflow |
| OpenClaw | ~/oss/openclaw |
| NemoClaw | ~/oss/NemoClaw |
| Slurm | ~/oss/slurm |

## Preferences

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Max open PRs per project | 10 |
| Max parallel PRs in development | 3 |
| Preferred issue types | bug, good first issue, help wanted |
| Skip issue types | RFC, platform-specific, security |
